7.4 MODEL ARCHITECTURE
───────────────────────

  MODEL A: Payment Days Predictor  [EXISTING — enhance]
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Type: Regression
  Target: days_to_pay (how many days from invoice date to payment)
  Algorithm: LightGBM (faster than XGBoost, handles large client-ID cardinality)
  
  Key Features:
  - client avg days to pay (last 12 months rolling)
  - client avg days to pay (last 3 months — detects behavior drift)
  - late_payment_rate (% paid after due date)
  - end_of_month_payer (bool — some clients always pay last 3 days)
  - quarter_end_payer (bool — clients that accelerate at QE)
  - invoice_amount (larger invoices may take longer to approve)
  - aging_bucket (how old is this invoice already?)
  - days_until_due (urgency factor)
  - currency (GBP/EUR/USD — different payment cultures)
  - entity_id (entity-specific payment patterns)
  - is_chapter11 (from client_rules — if True: days_to_pay → very high)
  - corrected_due_date_used (flag: was ATNA-style rule applied?)
  - month_of_year, is_quarter_end (seasonal)
  
  Enhancements needed (from self-review):
  → Add holiday-adjusted predicted payment date post-processing
  → Add corrected_due_date for ATNA/custom-rule clients as training feature
  → Recalculate days_to_pay in training data using corrected_due_dates
  → Handle cold-start clients (use entity type averages)

  MODEL B: Payment Amount Predictor  [NEW — critical gap]
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Stage 1: Classification — What type of payment?
    Classes: Full | Partial | Disputed | Written-off
    Algorithm: LightGBM Classifier with class weights (Full is majority)
    Key Features: same as Model A + dispute_rate + payment_pct_avg_historical

  Stage 2: Regression — How much % will be paid? (Partial class only)
    Target: payment_pct (0 to 1)
    Algorithm: LightGBM Regressor

  Combined:
    predicted_amount = invoice_amount × predicted_payment_pct
    For Full: pct = 1.0
    For Written-off / Disputed: pct = 0.0 (excluded from forecast)
    For Partial: pct = Stage 2 model output

  Lump-sum handling:
    If parent entity has on-account cash covering multiple child invoices:
    → Exclude child invoices from Model B prediction (already covered)
    → Show separately in dashboard under "On-Account Buffer"

  MODEL C: Days to Bill Predictor  [Phase 2 — data dependency]
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Input: Unbilled AR report + client + entity + service_date
  Target: days_until_billed (service_date → invoice_date)
  
