7.6 CHAPTER 11 / BAD DEBT HANDLING
──────────────────────────────────────

  [SELF-REVIEW FIX: Moved from Phase 3 to Phase 1 — this is critical]

  Problem: Our model currently treats ALL clients the same.
  A Chapter 11 client with £200K outstanding → model may predict "pays in 
  45 days" but the money will NEVER arrive (bankruptcy proceedings).

  If we include these in the forecast: we massively overstate cash.
  Treasury hedges for money that will never come → guaranteed loss.

  Solution:
  Step 1: Add is_chapter11 and is_dispute flags to client_rules table
  Step 2: Apply BEFORE running models: filter out flagged clients from forecast
  Step 3: Show them in a SEPARATE section: "Excluded from Forecast — Legal"
  Step 4: Track against the bad debt provision ($3M / ~1% of AR)
  Step 5: Alert if excluded amounts approach or exceed bad debt provision

  WHO MAINTAINS THIS FLAG:
  Finance team can update via dashboard settings (no developer needed)
  Monthly review: check if Chapter 11 clients have resolved / exited


