SECTION 10 — WHY THIS ARCHITECTURE IS THE RIGHT APPROACH
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

WHY TWO MODELS (Days + Amount) INSTEAD OF ONE?
  Different targets require different optimizations. Days = continuous 
  regression. Amount = classification first (what type of payment) then 
  regression (how much). One model would compromise both.

WHY LIGHTGBM OVER DEEP LEARNING?
  2 years of invoice data = typically 20K-100K rows. Too small for deep 
  learning to win. LightGBM: faster, interpretable, handles high-cardinality 
  categorical features (client IDs) natively. Finance team can see feature 
  importance: "Client X flagged because 3 invoices > 90 days in last year."

WHY RULE-BASED CLIENT TABLE INSTEAD OF HARDCODING ATNA?
  Every month there may be a new exception. Config table = database update, 
  not code change. Finance team can eventually manage it themselves.

WHY BUSINESS-DAY ADJUSTED FORECAST?
  Treasury hedges based on actual cash clearing. A payment "due Friday" 
  that falls on a bank holiday clears Monday — a 3-day timing error on 
  potentially millions of GBP. Small fix, material impact.

WHY CHAPTER 11 EXCLUSION IN PHASE 1 (NOT PHASE 3)?
  Including a Chapter 11 client in the forecast means predicting cash that 
  will NEVER arrive. This inflates the forecast and causes treasury to 
  over-hedge. A simple flag in the client table prevents this. It's 2 hours 
  of work but protects against major forecast errors.

WHY ON-ACCOUNT AS DISPLAY ADJUSTMENT (NOT AUTO-SETTLEMENT)?
  We don't know which invoices the on-account cash covers until finance 
  does manual matching. Auto-netting could assign it to wrong invoices. 
  Better to show it separately and let humans complete the match.

WHY KEEP MANUAL OVERRIDE?
  Current manual accuracy = 97-98%. Our model may initially be at 85-90%.
  Finance leads' domain knowledge will outperform the model in edge cases.
  Override logging creates a training signal: the model learns from human 
  corrections. Over time, model accuracy improves toward human-level.


