6.1 THE EXACT AETNA DATE CALCULATION RULE
───────────────────────────────────────────

  KEY UPDATE: The previous design said "count from 1st of invoice month."
  The images clarify it more precisely:

  "The calculation is service month is one day."
  "So let's say you are providing service for June."
  "They will calculate from 1st July, 1st July plus 75 days."
  → Aetna's term starts from the FIRST DAY OF THE MONTH AFTER SERVICE MONTH.

  EXAMPLE:
  Service provided: June (any date in June)
  Aetna term start: 1 July (first day of NEXT month)
  Payment due: 1 July + 75 days = 14 September

  CONTRAST WITH STANDARD:
  Invoice raised: June 15
  Standard due: June 15 + 75 = August 29
  Aetna due:    July 1 + 75  = September 14  (16 days LATER, not earlier!)

  CRITICAL CORRECTION FROM v2:
  Previous design said Aetna pays EARLIER. Images clarify they pay LATER
  than standard calculation because the term starts next month, not this month.

  "Whenever you bill a June invoice and then July, August, it doesn't matter.
   They will calculate from 1st July, 1st July plus 75 days."

6.2 WHERE TO APPLY THE AETNA CALCULATION
